# snifdog -- SNIF CA Transparency watchdog, cron mode.
#
# Run one incremental CT pass every 15 minutes for every configuration:
# /etc/snif/snifdog.conf if it exists, and each /etc/snif/snifdog.d/*.conf,
# normally one per base domain. Each configuration keeps its own state
# directory, and a pass whose previous run on the same configuration is still
# going skips quietly. To move a one-base install to the directory, move its
# snifdog.conf there (do not copy it), keeping its SNIFDOG_DIR.
#
# `snifdog poll` exits non-zero (2) when it raises a NEW alert, so cron mails
# the run output to MAILTO on a detection (in addition to snifdog's own syslog
# / webhook / email sinks).
#
# Use this instead of the systemd `snifdog watch` units, not alongside them.

MAILTO=root

*/15 * * * *  snif  for c in /etc/snif/snifdog.conf /etc/snif/snifdog.d/*.conf; do [ -r "$c" ] && SNIFDOG_CONF="$c" /usr/bin/snifdog poll; done
